{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents","id":695059,"title":"Can elementals create exigents?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-09T10:08:16-07:00","id":695059,"title":"Can elementals create exigents?","content":"Curious if there is an answer to this. And if not, what people think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T10:10:56-07:00","id":695086,"title":"","content":"The devs say &quot;No.&quot; While we're at it, it's also not possible for Demons, Fair Folk, or other Exalted to make exigents.<br /> <br /> I think this is a necessary limitation in order to prevent Exigence from being a kind of blank check to give anyone whatever just superpowers you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T10:15:02-07:00","id":695091,"title":"","content":"Makes sense, also-- there has never been, to my mind, sufficient difference between the two classes of spirit so I'm in favor of anything that distinguishes them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T10:22:45-07:00","id":695094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695091#post695091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes sense, also-- there has never been, to my mind, sufficient difference between the two classes of spirit so I'm in favor of anything that distinguishes them</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that a Dog of the Unbroken Earth has been cited as a potential creator of an Exigent is literally the only thing that reminds me that they're gods and not elementals.<br /> <br /> I mean, they're dogs! Of earth! Like cloud bears are bears of clouds! But those are elementals! Aaaaaah!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T10:29:58-07:00","id":695098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695091#post695091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes sense, also-- there has never been, to my mind, sufficient difference between the two classes of spirit so I'm in favor of anything that distinguishes them</div> </div> </div> </div>The devs seem to share this view. I'm encouraged by <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-exalted-3rd-edition/posts/884408\" target=\"_blank\">that Elementals KS preview</a> from a ways back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T10:33:00-07:00","id":695100,"title":"","content":"Everyone else beat me to it lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T10:41:31-07:00","id":695105,"title":"","content":"That said I bet if you want elementals or demons to have some weird way to Exalt people, the Exigents book will provide you with a good way to mechanically implement that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T10:53:19-07:00","id":695110,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the Elemental Dragons and the dragons that are elementals will be in any way related in this edition.<br /> <br /> That was a bit confusing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T11:01:02-07:00","id":695132,"title":"","content":"or the 8 different monsters all named kukla","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T11:06:28-07:00","id":695164,"title":"","content":"One of the issues with elementals being able to create Exigents is that everyone would make the Chosen of a lesser elemental dragon who is just a DB but with Solar-tier power. Gods tend to create more original and interesting Exigents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T11:09:03-07:00","id":695165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695132#post695132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or the 8 different monsters all named kukla</div> </div> </div> </div>Wha? Isn't there just the one Greater Elemental Dragon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T11:12:16-07:00","id":695180,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure there were two because of some kind of mistake","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T11:18:14-07:00","id":695184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695110#post695110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was a bit confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as confusing as the Lesser-Greater-Great Elemental Dragon thing.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping EX3 drops the &quot;Greater&quot; moniker, so it's just Great and Lesser, like in the 1e corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T11:23:13-07:00","id":695187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695180#post695180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure there were two because of some kind of mistake</div> </div> </div> </div>There was. One was an Elemental that ascended to greater poeer. The other, from DotFA (something else that book screwed up) was some sort of ctjonic god that was accidently released.<br /> <br /> Seems the writers of previous editions didnt talk to each other much when worldbuilding. I hope the current dev team is more careful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T11:26:52-07:00","id":695192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695164#post695164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the issues with elementals being able to create Exigents is that everyone would make the Chosen of a lesser elemental dragon who is just a DB but with Solar-tier power. Gods tend to create more original and interesting Exigents.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that doesn't really follow logically-- why would &quot;everyone&quot; do that? Who is &quot;everyone&quot;? Why is &quot;everyone&quot;'s storyteller being an ass. Also remember LED are single element beings so while they might overlap it's not like they will be pan-elemental like dbs. Anyway, more to the point I think the reason they can't is that the exigence flows from the most high through the celestial and terrestrial hierarchies-- elementals serve the celestial buereacracy but are not a part of it, they are a different order of beings from gods and therefore cannot channel the power which is unique to Gods. Also elementals lack purviews the way gods do, they might have jobs but gods literally are defined by their purpose and exalted are, at the baseline, instruments of purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T11:39:30-07:00","id":695209,"title":"","content":"I always distinguished them with capitalisation; lesser and greater elemental dragons compared with the Elemental Dragons. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aretii</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, they're dogs! Of earth! Like cloud bears are bears of clouds! But those are elementals! Aaaaaah!</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh come now, there are more substantial things to be confused about. Such as how tree gods are not wood elementals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T11:48:21-07:00","id":695213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aretii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695094#post695094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact that a Dog of the Unbroken Earth has been cited as a potential creator of an Exigent is literally the only thing that reminds me that they're gods and not elementals.<br /> <br /> I mean, they're dogs! Of earth! Like cloud bears are bears of clouds! But those are elementals! Aaaaaah!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Here's how I think of it: elementals are rarely as aggressive. An ifrit or a thunderbird is just gonna chill out, doing their thing, even if the thunderbird thing is to go smash somebody with your club for fun. They just follow their nature. A god, on the other hand, needs to protect their purview for spiritual and political reasons, so they're really get up in the grill of anyone who threatens them. Dogs of Unbroken Earth are gods of unsullied nature, so they get really mad when someone tries to sully nature. A comparable earth elemental would just get pissed that you're knocking down their house or whatever, or just be naturally rude to humans.<br /> I will say I'd like them to be less &quot;rock dog&quot; looking. Maybe incorporate wounds that look like footprints or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T11:53:19-07:00","id":695217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695105#post695105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said I bet if you want elementals or demons to have some weird way to Exalt people, the Exigents book will provide you with a good way to mechanically implement that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I plan to make an Exigent of my cat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T11:54:56-07:00","id":695218,"title":"","content":"So their powers would be based around cuteness, fuzziness, fickleness, hunting small animals, laziness, sleeping, and barf?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T12:01:35-07:00","id":695220,"title":"","content":"Their powers will be based around my cat's specific history, habits, and personality, not general 'catness.'<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T12:03:14-07:00","id":695223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695218#post695218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So their powers would be based around cuteness, fuzziness, fickleness, hunting small animals, laziness, sleeping, and barf?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget Chase The Red Dot Prana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T12:18:38-07:00","id":695227,"title":"","content":"While I also disagree with Lioness' assertion and some people might find it fun to come up with elaborate cosmological reasons behind the exclusivity of Exigence, it all strikes me as a bit post hoc. I think the simplest reason, both in and out of character, for it not to be used by demons and things, is to make Exigence something more than generic Exalted generator, namely something that interacts with and emerges out of the Celestial Bureaucracy (which also gets into its association with the Sidereal Exalted). To the extent that that signifies a distinction between gods and elementals, I think that could be a thing of elementals being kind of outside the Bureaucracy, especially if they're not really a designed servitor race to the gods anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T12:34:21-07:00","id":695235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695220#post695220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their powers will be based around my cat's specific history, habits, and personality, not general 'catness.'</div> </div> </div> </div>For the sake of trivia, is this the same Glorious Solar Kitty from before your Wonder Woman avatar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T13:05:53-07:00","id":695274,"title":"","content":"I suspect and hope that 3e DBs might be less pan-elemental and will have a design that allows them to express any ability through the power of their aspect element.<br /> <br /> I do love elementals but I am honestly having a hard time seeing how their Exigents would not heavily overlap with Dragon-Blooded. Exigents of a Cloud Prince, Gemlord or Garda Bird would be interesting but their powers ultimately fall within a similar elemental design space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T13:19:59-07:00","id":695282,"title":"","content":"Need Dragon Blooded who are elemental soldier-scholar-bureaucrats. Contrast passionate furious socialite warriors with Exalted built around themes of immolation and resurrection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T13:24:31-07:00","id":695288,"title":"","content":"Sure, but aside from the themes of resurrection all of that could apply to a Fire Aspect. Passionate socialite warrior? Sounds perfect. Themes of immolation? Comes with the territory.<br /> <br /> There are areas of focus elemental exigents could touch on that Dragon-Bloods do not already encompass, but I'm not sure they would be sufficiently different. I would have the same complaint about Ghost-Exigents and similarities to Liminals/Abyssals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T13:35:43-07:00","id":695320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695227#post695227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I also disagree with Lioness' assertion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which? I've naval gazed on aspects of 3e design a lot and now I'm worried people are taking me seriously. I don't even take me seriously.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T13:39:50-07:00","id":695321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are areas of focus elemental exigents could touch on that Dragon-Bloods do not already encompass, but I'm not sure they would be sufficiently different.</div> </div> </div> </div> Volcano Exalt. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which?</div> </div> </div> </div> This whole thing {gestures vaguely at last several posts about elemental Exalted being equivalent to Dragon Blooded}.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T13:47:23-07:00","id":695326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695192#post695192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean that doesn't really follow logically-- why would &quot;everyone&quot; do that? Who is &quot;everyone&quot;? Why is &quot;everyone&quot;'s storyteller being an ass. Also remember LED are single element beings so while they might overlap it's not like they will be pan-elemental like dbs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in practice rather than everyone, very few people would do that (make Solar level elemental Exalted). But like, more than zero, I guess.<br /> <br /> (Maybe a few that did would undermine the setting mythology of elemental power as a lesser sort of power than Celestial might or something, in their games? And that's important?)<br /> <br /> I dunno. I can see why the devs would want not, sort of, if I tilt my head a bit and narrow my eyes; OTOH, you could make an Exigent of Wayang the Black Puppet Mask or the Golden Lord and you'd have a lot of overlap with Endings Sidereals or Solars, potentially, and also break certain restrictions those Exalted labour under (certainly, imagining the idea of fateish Chosen who are different from the Sidereals we got pleases me, much as I like those Sidereals). So it can't just be some degree of overlap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T18:33:37-07:00","id":695578,"title":"","content":"If you think an Endings Sidereal would look the same as a hypothetical Chosen of Wayang, then I worry you might've received some very different Exalted books from me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T19:03:15-07:00","id":695582,"title":"","content":"Dragon Blooded have generally been presented more as super warrior-scholars with an elemental patina than as actual elemental masters like Benders, or superhero characters like Iceman or someone like Crocodile or Akainu from One Piece. Those sorts of characters serve as an inspiration, yes, but when you make an Air Aspect, you're not really going to be playing Storm from the X-men. Honestly I imagine that if you want to make a character based around an element, you'd be better with an Exigent of some elementally related god because Dragon Blooded have never really worked that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T19:10:50-07:00","id":695592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695582#post695582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon Blooded have generally been presented more as super warrior-scholars with an elemental patina than as actual elemental masters like Benders, or superhero characters like Iceman or someone like Crocodile or Akainu from One Piece. Those sorts of characters serve as an inspiration, yes, but when you make an Air Aspect, you're not really going to be playing Storm from the X-men. Honestly I imagine that if you want to make a character based around an element, you'd be better with an Exigent of some elementally related god because Dragon Blooded have never really worked that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as the Devs seem to be actually going to delve deeper in the elements than skills - and possibly use some of the never adapted charm sketches from 1e ST companion - into the new edition's run of the Dragon-blooded, I would say it's a wait and see case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-09-2015, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T19:18:36-07:00","id":695595,"title":"","content":"I would allow any spirit of sufficient power to create one but that's just me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T19:44:16-07:00","id":695613,"title":"","content":"The idea is that the Unconquered Sun is the one actually doing the exalting. He's just using the god's essence to exalt a mortal instead of his own.<br /> <br /> As to why he only allows this of gods... I don't know. I can understand him not wanting to do it for demons but powerful elementals would seem to fit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695235#post695235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the sake of trivia, is this the same Glorious Solar Kitty from before your Wonder Woman avatar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all. This is devilcat, my black and gold kitty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T00:15:48-07:00","id":695835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695578#post695578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you think an Endings Sidereal would look the same as a hypothetical Chosen of Wayang, then I worry you might've received some very different Exalted books from me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must've received the versions of the books where Wayang was a powerful god over the fate of Endings, whose chosen might reasonably be expected to wield that power. <br /> <br /> I don't think I received the version of the books in which &quot;overlap&quot; was redefined to mean &quot;the same&quot; though. <br /> <br /> (Nor the ones where someone would specifically talk about Chosen of Gods of Fate who will be different from Sidereals and then be responded to with &quot;if you think they will be the same&quot; for some reason.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T02:45:07-07:00","id":695905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Devs seem to be actually going to delve deeper in the elements than skills</div> </div> </div> </div> Where do you get that? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must've received the versions of the books where Wayang was a powerful god over the fate of Endings</div> </div> </div> </div> That's a bureaucratic position, not an essential element. Wayang is a shadow puppet who is god over Silence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T02:50:42-07:00","id":695908,"title":"","content":"I'm going to be really interested in how the Exigents book presents models for Charms that are extremely novel in structure; things following the lead of volcanic Pressure, of Getimians having two mote pools that provide different effects when powering the same Charms, for the basic conceits of the Sidereal Charm cascades, hell even the intertwining trees of Second Edition Infernals. All the ways you could make Exalted function and <i>feel</i> different that largely overrides any surface level imagery, so there's something more to the difference between the fiery scion of a bloodline of heroes and the chosen of a continuously self-immolating and reviving beloved bird of fire than the colour of their fire special effects being a bit different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T03:07:52-07:00","id":695916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695905#post695905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Where do you get that? That's a bureaucratic position, not an essential element. Wayang is a shadow puppet who is god over Silence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we really not think the chosen of a god who is one of the heads of the Bureau of Fate will have power over that area of fate, in a general manner, as an inheritance of his essence? Do we think that god lacks special insight and command over the area of his bureaucratic office? Have his capabilities been delineated carefully in a way which would demonstrate he lacks such command?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T04:27:04-07:00","id":695926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695321#post695321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This whole thing {gestures vaguely at last several posts about elemental Exalted being equivalent to Dragon Blooded}.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think an Exigent created by an Elemental could be done well but I believe you'd also see a lot of concepts born from Second Edition's extremely reductive notions of Dragon-Blooded. People were saying &quot;Infernals don't exist in my Creation&quot; over less than this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T05:14:32-07:00","id":695976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695905#post695905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Devs seem to be actually going to delve deeper in the elements than skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do you get that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, i can't deny i choose my words badly here, sorry....<br /> Let me if i can express myself better this time around.<br /> <br /> &quot;From what few comments i've seen so far on DBs in 3e, the Devs seem to have shown some interest in Terrestrial charms that break away a little with the one skill/one element mold they usually follow since 1e Exalted: DB. The 1e ST Companion also had some interesting charm concepts that might fit on this, so, depending on how things pan out in the end (early intents can change considerably when one starts to tinker and work out the kinks &amp; etc), we might get some material for those who would like dragon-blooded with a bit more bender to them. It's wait and see i guess.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, if one asks for specific dev commentary on terrestrial charms out of the one skill/one element mold, i'll admit i haven't been much of a forum regular in the past few months and would have no idea of what topics to look for - if someone does remember something along those lines, i would appreciate any links/references.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T05:59:38-07:00","id":695997,"title":"","content":"So.......is there any ways to decide how much Elementally should a DB charm has when you homebrew stuffs for them ? Just go with your guts ?<br /> <br /> And when people say that DB will be less about elemental in Ex3, do you guy mean &quot;He's super hot, just like fire&quot; symbolism elemental or is it &quot;He's super hot, 'cause he's on fire&quot; physical elemental ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T08:32:23-07:00","id":696094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695164#post695164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the issues with elementals being able to create Exigents is that everyone would make the Chosen of a lesser elemental dragon who is just a DB but with Solar-tier power. Gods tend to create more original and interesting Exigents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then it's on the ST to hit them in the face with an orichalcum-plated corebook while yelling &quot;CHICANERY-NO!!!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T08:38:06-07:00","id":696097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695326#post695326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OTOH, you could make an Exigent of . . . the Golden Lord and you'd have a lot of overlap with . . . Solars, potentially, and also break certain restrictions those Exalted labour under</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Reading Blood &amp; Salt, you see the Golden Lord is tied to some pretty interesting themes (some of which are defined by his duality with the Pale Mistress). I wouldn't expect more than a superficial anima resemblance to Solars (which would certainly get a Golden Lord Exigent into trouble with the Immaculates) but very little beyond that. Solars don't have to be good guys while id say, categorically, by the god's very nature, the Golden Lord's Exigent would be a good and positive-virtuous person whose Charms might even revolve around that in ways Solar Charms certainly do not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T09:02:38-07:00","id":696139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=696097#post696097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. Reading Blood &amp; Salt, you see the Golden Lord is tied to some pretty interesting themes (some of which are defined by his duality with the Pale Mistress). I wouldn't expect more than a superficial anima resemblance to Solars (which would certainly get a Golden Lord Exigent into trouble with the Immaculates) but very little beyond that. Solars don't have to be good guys while id say, categorically, by the god's very nature, the Golden Lord's Exigent would be a good and positive-virtuous person whose Charms might even revolve around that in ways Solar Charms certainly do not.</div> </div> </div> </div>You disagree there'd be any overlap, or lots? In my opinion, of course there would be distinctions, with strong themes of judgement and insight which are more prominent for him than the Unconquered Sun, restrictions in ability to act against pain and suffering directly (which his chosen may or may not share strongly), themes of advising without ruling... yet also overlap with thematics of light, excellence, divine punishment and order. I wouldn't personally envision an Exigent of his as having any element of moral compulsion or restrictions to their excellence - it would be more interesting if he could have &quot;bad&quot; children who are still recognisably his children. I wouldn't consider it interesting for chosen of gods we'd consider to be negative to be constricted that way either. Particularly as he's obviously conceptually distinct as a god even if he does not pass on any moral aspect.<br /> <br /> Feel free to disagree by all means - I'm sure Exigents will be fun because many can interpret the same's god's chosen in different ways.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T10:33:37-07:00","id":696241,"title":"","content":"I disagree that, in the ways that some themes might overlap, that there wouldn't be ways to make them very mechanically distinct such that the actual overlap is minimal to nonexistent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T11:05:00-07:00","id":696251,"title":"","content":"I don't feel like mechanical or &quot;actual&quot; overlap as opposed to theme overlap was something I was talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T12:34:35-07:00","id":696386,"title":"","content":"I'm worried about exigents too, but on the other hand it would be a way to make an elemental warrior scion whos a bad enough dude to rescue the president if you were in a mixed circle. Really the DBs are so far away from their patrons anyway that it's not that hard to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T14:40:34-07:00","id":696501,"title":"","content":"Some of the worry about Exigents makes the most sense at the &quot;super-powered D&amp;D&quot; end of the Exalted spectrum. The more a group values the conflicts and structures of the setting (and I'm not saying that's the one right way to play) the less an Exigent can steal the role of an existing splat.<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blooded are the scions of the world's greatest empire, and no exigent of an elemental god can touch that. Obviously there are games in which that doesn't really matter, though I don't think Ex3 should be written around the premise that some groups won't care. I mean, if the narrative of a Realm nobles or an ambitious Outcaste doesn't do anything for you, sure, don't play a DB. Even without exigents on the table, if the DBs' only value is &quot;fire-punch dudes&quot; then you're happier playing something else. In a mixed group of DBs and exigents, the exigent might have some more impressive elemental charms, but he won't have the same role in Realm politics or society or the military, he won't join the Immaculate Order, and while he may be an ally to a sworn brotherhood, he's still an outsider helping out with a thing that DBs do.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals are the Five-Score Fellowship, and no exigent of any god, no matter how prominently placed in Yu Shan, will ever change that to the Five-Score-and-One Fellowship. Or if you want some big-picture mechanical differences, there's SMA, sorcery, astrology, and resplendent destinies to think about too. And despite some significant flaws in 2e's Heaven, I think we'll have a new version that will be a lot more inviting to interact with as a Sidereal. An exigent of Wayang would have a completely different role than a Sidereal - the Chosen of the Maidens are focused on righting Creation, but if Wayang wants to exalt someone, I'd expect his focus to be on problems in Heaven, where I'm sure that exigent would be as popular as 2e's Sids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T22:05:52-07:00","id":696775,"title":"","content":"Root makes good points, if you're playing a solar game though, most of those go by the wayside. You can slot almost any exigent into a solar story and have it work. It's actually one of the bemefits of solar stories, they're suuuuper flexible. You can do almost anything with them too, but maybe not exactly how you want to or how you want it to look, that's when exigents become appealing and I fear that might happen all too often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T01:32:47-07:00","id":696853,"title":"","content":"Nah, Solars still have a very specific storyline and place in the world history. Players just have to want to be them and take part in that. Which if the history of 50% of games being Solar only and a further 40% mainly Solar would show they do. So long as no one offloads more mechanical work on the ST as you fear, who is losing out from offering more flexibility for players who do not wish to glow gold or even care about the Solar story and style?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T06:05:29-07:00","id":696982,"title":"","content":"Wayang is invoked in prayers by the Shadow Puppeteers in the Shore Lands of An-Teng when they assign orders to their assassin-spirits. I would go absolutely wild with that for an Exigent of his.<br /> <br /> Less sure what I would do with the Golden Lord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T12:16:53-07:00","id":697682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=696982#post696982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Less sure what I would do with the Golden Lord.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Golden Lord is tricky because he already has a very Solar feel to him. He is a Solomon-like judge-king and lawgiver. <br /> <br /> I suppose powers focused around binding social injunctions and being empowered by upholding the rule of law would be appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T13:05:37-07:00","id":697805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695976#post695976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, i can't deny i choose my words badly here, sorry....<br /> Let me if i can express myself better this time around.<br /> <br /> &quot;From what few comments i've seen so far on DBs in 3e, the Devs seem to have shown some interest in Terrestrial charms that break away a little with the one skill/one element mold they usually follow since 1e Exalted: DB. The 1e ST Companion also had some interesting charm concepts that might fit on this, so, depending on how things pan out in the end (early intents can change considerably when one starts to tinker and work out the kinks &amp; etc), we might get some material for those who would like dragon-blooded with a bit more bender to them. It's wait and see i guess.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, if one asks for specific dev commentary on terrestrial charms out of the one skill/one element mold, i'll admit i haven't been much of a forum regular in the past few months and would have no idea of what topics to look for - if someone does remember something along those lines, i would appreciate any links/references.</div> </div> </div> </div>The quotes I read were along the lines of &quot;Playing an air-aspected melee fighter felt like playing a wannabe fire-aspect, because melee is a fire skill. Let's change that so that you can show your element in whatever skill you pick to excel in.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nothing about bending, just more than one element per skill. Maybe the skill trees will branch out into various elemental branches, but that still has nothing to do with bending. Heck, if they have elemental-neutral roots, it could be even less bendy than before.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T13:16:33-07:00","id":697826,"title":"","content":"Where do people get that most, or even any, Exigents are Solar tier? Unless a very powerful god is willing to sacrifice a lot of his power, this won't ever be... Most Exigencies will have to get UCS approval too, so there is that also.<br /> <br /> Even if a greater elemental could (and according to the devs and canon they can't) and sacrificed himself wholly to the Exigency I don't believe the result would be a Solar Tier Exalt, probably be a Terrestrial level or maybe a bit more.<br /> <br /> I don't know, this is all speculation, but from what we were told Solars are still King of the Hill. And unless you can come up with a story, and the ST approves (and through him, UCS), that explains why such a highly powered god is willing to give up so much of his power (maybe even his life) so you can have this power, your Exigent won't be anywhere near Celestial, much less Solar, tier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T13:28:06-07:00","id":697841,"title":"","content":"That's reasonable. Certainly, in universe (opposed to some particular game), most Exigents are not gonna be very strong, to the extent that kind of tier thinking even applies, and there's not many of them.<br /> <br /> At the same time, God moves in mysterious ways, as they say. Why God chooses some for a great destiny and others not, is not necessarily exactly the sort of thing amenable to being rationally justified (if you believe in that sort of thing).<br /> <br /> Given how little of why the UCS has chosen some individual Solar is going to be explained - some people just impress him, or speak to his soul, for whatever reasons, ultimately ones that, to be Doylist, suit you game - I think it's a bit much to require players to explain necessarily and justify why he chooses to grant some Exigent a lot more juice than others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T13:38:52-07:00","id":697868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=697826#post697826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do people get that most, or even any, Exigents are Solar tier?</div> </div> </div> </div>No one has said 'most,' the developers have said that the Exigents can be as powerful as Solars.<br /> <br /> It's good to remember that the power curve for 3rd Edition isn't the same as 2nd and 'tiers' aren't a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T13:39:12-07:00","id":697869,"title":"","content":"The Devs have said that Exigents range from less mighty than Terrestrials to equally as mighty as Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T14:31:34-07:00","id":697919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=697841#post697841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how little of why the UCS has chosen some individual Solar is going to be explained - some people just impress him, or speak to his soul, for whatever reasons, ultimately ones that, to be Doylist, suit you game - I think it's a bit much to require players to explain necessarily and justify why he chooses to grant some Exigent a lot more juice than others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in my point of view, why you were Exalted is a much bigger point in a Exigent's story that in a Solar's. The UCS did what he did and now a finite number of Solar Exaltations are around and happening for mysterious reasons as he works in mysterious ways. An Exigency has a much more defined purpose than that, and I don't think it is too much to require a player to justify why a god went through so much to grant his powers.<br /> <br /> If you want to play a Chosen of Death but can't come up with why Thanatos, Supreme God of Death, cut a out a hefty chunk of his soul to empower you then you are going to be the Chosen of Mr Gravedirt, God of Those Who Died When They Were Burying Another Person. And your power level is Terrestrial, at best.<br /> <br /> If you want to play &quot;I don't know why i have these powers, I just know its awesome!&quot; There are many splats for that already.<br /> <br /> Thats just me as an ST though. Nothing wrong If you are fine with that for your players. I have a group thats been playing together for over a decade (not Exalted though), and they know that setting consistency is a big deal, and they also know not to expect me to come up with their backstories, I can help, but thats part of their contribution to the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=697868#post697868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No one has said 'most,' the developers have said that the Exigents can be as powerful as Solars.<br /> <br /> It's good to remember that the power curve for 3rd Edition isn't the same as 2nd and 'tiers' aren't a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=697868#post697868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No one has said 'most,' the developers have said that the Exigents can be as powerful as Solars.<br /> <br /> It's good to remember that the power curve for 3rd Edition isn't the same as 2nd and 'tiers' aren't a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is mainly directed at the people who are saying &quot;No ones gonna play Solars anymore, every spirit and their mother can Exalt Exigents, and they're SOLAR TIER!&quot; Which is not true. To get your champion to the level of a Solar you have to be a mighty god and sacrifice a significant portion of your power and submit to the UCS for approval and pay his price. Most gods can't afford a Solar Tier Exigency, not even if they give their whole existence in return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T14:48:12-07:00","id":697983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=697919#post697919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is mainly directed at the people who are saying &quot;No ones gonna play Solars anymore, every spirit and their mother can Exalt Exigents, and they're SOLAR TIER!&quot; Which is not true. To get your champion to the level of a Solar you have to be a mighty god and sacrifice a significant portion of your power and submit to the UCS for approval and pay his price. Most gods can't afford a Solar Tier Exigency, not even if they give their whole existence in return.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that people with this concern are approaching it from a doylist perspective. That is, it's not that most exigents in the setting will be solar-level, it's that most players will want their exigent to be solar-level, because unless they have a specific play experience in mind that requires them to be weaker, players tend to gravitate towards whatever gives them the most power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/91-wandering","name":"Wandering","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar91_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T15:06:15-07:00","id":697987,"title":"","content":"I'd phrase it, mostly similarly in meaning, that probably people key to a level of power that's similar to the rest of their group, rather than automatically go for the most (although people being people most probably would try to edge it up as much as possible without blatantly irritating everyone).<br /> <br /> If you're playing a group of mortal Sorcerers they're gonna design an Exigent one way, Outcaste adventurers another, a Solar Circle another again. Guess which of these three scenarios is more common?<br /> <br /> I suspect &quot;You need a really, really good reason not to be generally around Dragonblooded power level at most&quot; is not always gonna be a fun response to someone playing an Exigent in a Solar Circle; &quot;You need a real good reason to have Solar Circle Sorcery (or anything else particularly particular to the Solar Exalted rather than general to Celestials)&quot; probably is more generally OK.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T15:28:09-07:00","id":697996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=697919#post697919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in my point of view, why you were Exalted is a much bigger point in a Exigent's story that in a Solar's. The UCS did what he did and now a finite number of Solar Exaltations are around and happening for mysterious reasons as he works in mysterious ways. An Exigency has a much more defined purpose than that, and I don't think it is too much to require a player to justify why a god went through so much to grant his powers.<br /> <br /> If you want to play a Chosen of Death but can't come up with why Thanatos, Supreme God of Death, cut a out a hefty chunk of his soul to empower you then you are going to be the Chosen of Mr Gravedirt, God of Those Who Died When They Were Burying Another Person. And your power level is Terrestrial, at best.<br /> <br /> That is mainly directed at the people who are saying &quot;No ones gonna play Solars anymore, every spirit and their mother can Exalt Exigents, and they're SOLAR TIER!&quot; Which is not true. To get your champion to the level of a Solar you have to be a mighty god and sacrifice a significant portion of your power and submit to the UCS for approval and pay his price. Most gods can't afford a Solar Tier Exigency, not even if they give their whole existence in return.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may not necessarily be true (the part about a god having to sacrifice much to call a &quot;greater&quot; Exigent, for all we know, the god has ZERO say over the power of its Chosen; a top-tier god might have a &quot;weaker&quot; Exigent than a field god, but the point with 3e really is that power tier dick-measuring is unfun, so why stress over this?<br /> <br /> I really dislike the notion that a &quot;weak&quot; god can only make a &quot;weak&quot; Exigent. Ten Sheaves was, by all info available, a pretty minor god, but Janest doesn't appear to be weak by any stretch.<br /> <br /> Really, I think this will largely be an OOC issue. A Solar group where one person is an Exigent, should probably not be markedly weaker than the Solars unless they have depth of power rivaling or equaling them in some field (incidentally, this is apparently going to be the case with DBs, where DBs can rarely do things that are as or more powerful than Solars, but only in certain contexts and not broadly).<br /> <br /> As I have said, context is everything. If someone asks, &quot;Why haven't all the Exigents in history been as strong as Solars, if my character can be&quot; the only real relevant in-setting answer is &quot;Because Exaltation is a divine miracle that cannot be deeply understood with rational thought alone.&quot; I feel as if that is a sufficient explanation and anyone demanding more should be reminded that 3e is not going to categorically try to define every little tiny mystery (thank god). And Exigents were super rare throughout history; if they're stronger now, the world must really need them, neh?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=697841#post697841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a bit much to require players to explain necessarily and justify why he chooses to grant some Exigent a lot more juice than others.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it has to do with the &quot;volume&quot; of the Exigence bestowed at all. It's simply a miracle. If people want an explanation as to &quot;why X god's Exigent is stronger than N god's,&quot; well, tough shit, an explanation isn't needed. It's just what happened. In Creation, there's not always a reason that can be riddled out. That's the cool thing about miracles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 10-11-2015, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T15:43:33-07:00","id":698008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is mainly directed at the people who are saying &quot;No ones gonna play Solars anymore, every spirit and their mother can Exalt Exigents, and they're SOLAR TIER!&quot; Which is not true. To get your champion to the level of a Solar you have to be a mighty god and sacrifice a significant portion of your power and submit to the UCS for approval and pay his price. Most gods can't afford a Solar Tier Exigency, not even if they give their whole existence in return.</div> </div> </div> </div> What are you basing this on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T16:09:28-07:00","id":698037,"title":"","content":"Sometimes powerful gods will make Exigents weaker than Terrestrial's. And sometimes a weak god will make an Exigent who can rival the Solar Exalted. The gift of Exigence is a divine miracle that surpasses understanding, and therefore allows both STs and PCs wide latitude when creating Exigents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T17:20:02-07:00","id":698149,"title":"","content":"I'm basing it on the Law of Diminishment. There is no free lunch. No something for nothing.<br /> <br /> Its not about dick measuring its about setting consistency. If any low grade god can just sacrifice himself to get a Solar champion (when he was about to be destroyed anyways or out of duty, pick whichever motivation you think moved Ten Sheaves to Exalt the Strawmaiden) things would be out of order pretty soon.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying its impossible (nothing ever is, fantasy rpg being what we're discussing here).<br /> <br /> It might be how my perspective was colored from what I read, and then distorted by how long its been since I read it. But my view of the Exigency is that it is a grave matter for the god that is requesting it. It has a price and it must be paid. And to me that is a very big part of what being an Exigent is. It can create many story hooks about fulfillment of that purpose, or reneging it. About duty and responsibility or disappointment and regret, but it is a part of the story.<br /> <br /> Maybe Strawmaiden is Solar level. But then it was because The UCS saw that the cause was righteous and he infused her with some of his power, maybe her Exaltation will last only that battle with the Fair Folk and then she will die or be drained of her powers... Who knows?<br /> <br /> Solars is &quot;you were this kind of person and you needed power to change the world, The UCS somehow agreed with you for a moment and now you have that power, what do you do?&quot; The UCS can be nonchalant about his champions. He paid the price long ago, if one somehow goes wrong there are many others, and eventually the investment will be able to be remade when the bad one goes away. He is a multibillionaire investing in start-ups, stocks and currency, throwing his weight around to make shit happen. He can give you a bunch of money, and say make me proud. His money is magical and the only cost he will have is the opportunity cost.<br /> <br /> Exigent is &quot;Somegod really needed someshit done and somehow the best (and most of the time, only) way to do it was by giving you this power. He really cut a piece of (or even sacrificed) himself for you to be what you are now and do this for him. What do you do?&quot; That god is most likely like a desperate gambler who just put his rent money on Horse #9. Or a small business owner who took on a second mortgage to open a new storefront. It is a significant investment, and returns are not only expected, they are needed. They won't just give you that money. They most likely won't get it back. They need you to do this.<br /> <br /> Can The UCS say &quot;Hey buddy, I see that you are betting your rent money because your daughter has cancer and needs this medicine for this week. Tell you what I'll match your rent money with a million bucks, if you win she won't have to worry about it ever again.&quot; Yes, He can. That is why backstory matters, and in the games that I ST, will certainly be mandatory for the specially special snowflake.<br /> <br /> Why you were Exalted is a much greater part of your story as an Exigent than as a Solar.<br /> <br /> Having any half-assed god produce a champion to rival the Most Powerful Evah Godkings of Yore<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\">\u2122 <span style=\"font-size:14px\">and the reason being &quot;Miraclez!&quot; cheapens the Exigency, Exaltation in general, and the setting as a whole, in my humble opinion, that is.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Like I said in my previous post, my views, and all speculation.<br /> <br /> If you think its cool, more power to ya. No one is gonna stomp on your fun, there is no badwrongfun after all. But if you are worried that your players are going to all want to be Solar Power Chosen of Other Gods (presumably without the whole Anathema and Great Curse deal, which is to be seen), there are plenty of in setting reasons to put a stop to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 10-11-2015, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T20:16:02-07:00","id":698329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=698149#post698149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its not about dick measuring its about setting consistency.</div> </div> </div> </div>there is no consistency at a baseline<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=698149#post698149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Strawmaiden is Solar level. But then it was because The UCS saw that the cause was righteous and he infused her with some of his power, maybe her Exaltation will last only that battle with the Fair Folk and then she will die or be drained of her powers...</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots of assumptions here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=698149#post698149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can The UCS say &quot;Hey buddy, I see that you are betting your rent money because your daughter has cancer and needs this medicine for this week. Tell you what I'll match your rent money with a million bucks, if you win she won't have to worry about it ever again.&quot; Yes, He can. That is why backstory matters, and in the games that I ST, will certainly be mandatory for the specially special snowflake.<br /> <br /> Why you were Exalted is a much greater part of your story as an Exigent than as a Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're ascribing a level of control over the &quot;power&quot; granted by the Exigence not borne out by what we know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=698149#post698149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> there are plenty of in setting reasons to put a stop to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah I consider the handwringing over &quot;omg Exigents being Solar power SO BORKED!!!&quot; to be totally OOC baseless Chicken Littling by people who refuse to acknowledge context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T20:48:11-07:00","id":698356,"title":"","content":"All here is actually assumptions, suppositions, speculations and extrapolations, right? Or do we have a definitive source on Exigents?<br /> <br /> The Law of Diminishment, is basically your no free lunch clause, and the basis of much of what I think on the subject. The power has to come from somewhere. If he that is granting the power had no control over how much was given it would probably only happen as death throes, and since that not the case you can extrapolate from there. <br /> <br /> What is harder to do is figure out the ratio of Godpower Loss to Exalted Power, supposing it is not zero sum.<br /> <br /> But the most powerful god in the setting who was an ever present entity on the sky, now sets everyday. The UCS gave up a lot for his champions, and thats The UCS. He was greatly diminished by that, being subject to the law.<br /> <br /> Now, what would a god orders of magnitude weaker than The UCS have to give up to Exalt someone? How powerful could that god alone make that champion?<br /> <br /> I don't know, I can only extrapolate from what was given and discuss that with those who would entertain my ideas and whose ideas entertain me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T21:43:47-07:00","id":698392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=698356#post698356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If he that is granting the power had no control over how much was given it would probably only happen as death throes, and since that not the case you can extrapolate from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>... I'm not sure I understand your assumption. Are you saying that if gods have no control, they'll only use it if they're actively dying? This really doesn't strike me as reasonable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the most powerful god in the setting who was an ever present entity on the sky, now sets everyday. The UCS gave up a lot for his champions, and thats The UCS. He was greatly diminished by that, being subject to the law. </div> </div> </div>The Sun also created 300 Chosen who will reincarnate ceaselessly in the process, instead of (typically) a single one who might not reincarnate at all. Noteworthy also is the following remark from the lead developer: combined with earlier remarks, an Exigent can be as powerful as a Solar, but will not also be as broad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short answer is that every Exigent is a different kind of Exalt so they will have varying capabilities. There are structural limitations, however. You can't make an Exigent that is as broad and as powerful as a Solar, or an Exigent of destiny and fate that is everything a Sidereal is and more.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What is harder to do is figure out the ratio of Godpower Loss to Exalted Power, supposing it is not zero sum.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Now, what would a god orders of magnitude weaker than The UCS have to give up to Exalt someone? How powerful could that god alone make that champion? </div> </div> </div>It's worth noting that the Celestial Incarnae specifically did not use the Divine Exigence to create their Exalted. For this reason, I'd caution against making too many assumptions about similarities in the process. Not that &quot;giving up something is necessary&quot; is at all unreasonable, mind, just making note of it.<br /> <br /> What <i>is</i> unreasonable is assuming there is precisely one ratio in play. This need not be the case at all. Different gods could have different rates of exchange, as could different instances or circumstances of creating an Exigent.<br /> <br /> Basically, if you have a problem with it being a miracle, the process at your table can be as arbitrarily complicated as you need it to be to satisfy you. All of this is happening under the hood for the sake of the world, the game, and the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Minor tweak. 10-12-2015, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T22:37:12-07:00","id":698405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=698392#post698392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I'm not sure I understand your assumption. Are you saying that if gods have no control, they'll only use it if they're actively dying? This really doesn't strike me as reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. If you don't <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>*know*</b></span> if doing something will leave you either winded, permanently disabled or dead, how likely are you to do it unless you are in immediate risk of death or dying?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=698392#post698392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sun also created 300 Chosen in the process instead of (typically) a single one. Noteworthy also is the following remark from the lead developer: combined with earlier remarks, an Exigent can be as powerful as a Solar, but will not also be as broad.</div> </div> </div> </div>And why do you think or suggest that is? If it is such an unknowable miracle that we can't even wax cheap philosophy about it, why have any restrictions at all? Its a miracle! Elementals and demons can do it too! Shit, who knows I might be able to myself, its a miracle afterall!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=698392#post698392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that the Celestial Incarnae specifically did not use the Divine Exigence to create their Exalted. For this reason, I'd caution against making too many assumptions about similarities in the process. Not that &quot;giving up something is necessary&quot; is at all unreasonable, mind, just making note of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have the mention of the Law of Diminishment with mention of the first Exaltations and Ten Sheaves' apparent sacrifice to go on... What else? What is wrong with speculating on assumptions and extrapolations of that? We have crumbs to play with. Even when the book is out, there is still the possibility that these matters are left unclear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=698392#post698392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What <i>is</i> unreasonable is assuming there is precisely one ratio in play. This need not be the case at all. Different gods could have different rates of exchange, as could different instances or circumstances of creating an Exigent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree.<br /> <br /> &quot;What is harder to do is figure out the ratio of Godpower Loss to Exalted Power, supposing it is not zero sum.&quot; Quoting myself here. There could be many ratios, many situations, I agree... All I did was invite people to think about how it happened before. Maybe the only direct example is Ten Sheaves sacrifice to Exalt Janest. What little is presented shows some sort of structure. There is a price that has to be paid. And it is steep.<br /> <br /> You are very welcome to assume otherwise, and if you would like to share why you think that is I'm reading!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=698392#post698392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, if you have a problem with it being a miracle, the process at your table can be as arbitrarily complicated as you need it to be to satisfy you. All of this is happening under the hood for the sake of the world, the game, and the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>My only problem with that is that it leaves little to discuss. Its like trying to have a conversation about the Holy Trinity with a Catholic priest, &quot;Its a Mystery&quot;... Well ok!<br /> <br /> Anybody can do whatever they want in their table, thats a given. Canon is only true as long as it fits my story. I come to the forums to get ideas, try to discuss and hopefully temper my ideas and notions and hopefully strengthen my understanding of the setting for when its time to play.<br /> <br /> The process in your table can be as arbitrarily simple as you need it to be to satisfy you.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">EDIT</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 10-12-2015, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T02:22:33-07:00","id":698462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=698149#post698149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why you were Exalted is a much greater part of your story as an Exigent than as a Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why you were Exalted is a much greater part of their story than a whole bunch of caveats and conditions and costs.<br /> <br /> This impulse some people are having to view the possibilities inherent in Exigents in terms of &quot;we need to precisely break down every little part in order to figure out the precise sources and values of every component with which we can build our Exalted and their powers&quot; is quite off putting to me, whether it's in terms of &quot;oh, we need to know the exact costs required to get an Exigent with might comparable to that of a Solar&quot; or &quot;oh, we need to figure out the precise formula of divinity and personality and circumstances you would need in order to get an Exigent that is indistinguishable from another kind of Exalt, particularly so we can complain about this abstruse convergence existing to devalue the things we like&quot;.<br /> <br /> If that leaves little to discuss about such a marginal element of actual gameplay, let alone setting, than all the better for it. It may help certain kinds of people focus on their story and character rather than all of these things a microscope or theology doctorate is required for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T04:42:51-07:00","id":698497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=697868#post697868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No one has said 'most,' the developers have said that the Exigents can be as powerful as Solars.<br /> <br /> It's good to remember that the power curve for 3rd Edition isn't the same as 2nd and 'tiers' aren't a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They said tiers were not a thing. They also said Solars were still the most powerful Exalts, and those inclined to search for certain things on the internet can in fact confirm that from...sources. The &quot;no tiers&quot; thing is a recognition that they are reducing the gulf between the various types, and an acknowledgement that the terms &quot;Celestial&quot; and &quot;Terrestrial&quot; are increasingly unhelpful in a world that is growing to include Liminals, Getimians, etc.<br /> <br /> Exigents do not exist to subvert the narrative of Solars as the mighty returning god-kings who have tremendous power. They exist to allow people to tell stories of truly unique Exalts. Now, in service to that story, as Ghosthead mentioned, it may make sense to have a given Exigent be nearly as powerful, or as powerful, as Solars. I'm rolling around that possibility in my game at the moment. But, that doesn't mean we should in the standard setting that many, most, or even a significant minority of Exigents will equal Solars. That would also make them more powerful overall than Sidereals, Lunars, etc, and that's an undesirable game state for a multitude of reasons.<br /> <br /> &quot;My Exigent was actually created by the sacrifice of the Sixth Maiden, so he's as powerful as a Solar. Oh, and he's laser-proof and invisible,&quot; is going to happen, and it will be up to the STs, hopefully with guidance from the book, to dial all that back.<br /> <br /> I'm also not too worried because at the rate we are going Exigents won't be out until 2020. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T07:15:50-07:00","id":698612,"title":"","content":"People keep mistaking the thing with tiers, right down to misquoting it.<br /> <br /> They've never said that tiers aren't a thing; they say that it is not a terminology they use internally and that they discourage people who play the game from using, because it is reductive and leads to incorrect conclusions.<br /> <br /> Different Exalted are more and less powerful than each other under comparable circumstances. Focusing on that in terms of fighting game tournament terminology distracts people from things including how often gameplay consists of non-comparable circumstances. Thinking of things in terms of &quot;Solar tier&quot; and &quot;Terrestrial tier&quot; eliminates consideration of things like the newly Exalted versus the Wyld Hunt, or a lone elder, or the collected and organised distribution of the resources of the Realm, and it makes people confused about how to clot in complete non-comparables such as Alchemical modularity, Lunar shapeshifting, or Liminal resurrection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T08:09:24-07:00","id":698626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=698356#post698356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Law of Diminishment, is basically your no free lunch clause, and the basis of much of what I think on the subject. The power has to come from somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're reading crunch into fluff, which is always a dangerous prospect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=698356#post698356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If he that is granting the power had no control over how much was given it would probably only happen as death throes</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh...no? Considering how we have a handful of examples if that, and there's been no mention of dirty bombs diminishing the several spirits contributing to one. I don't think your extrapolation is appropriate or based in fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T11:20:35-07:00","id":698809,"title":"","content":"Isator, I don't follow the whole caveat, condition and cost thing. All I'm saying is that a god suffered greatly to be able to throw an Exigent at his problem. And you (the Exigent's player) should be able to expand on why either a very powerful god would go through this or how a minor god's concerns merit such a potent blessing. The player should have a backstory for his Exaltation through Exigency that makes sense, unlike playing one of the other splats. And thats at my table, like I said before. I play with the same people for a long time and they know they can't just throw super generic stuff at me and expect a super cool and involved story in return, I'm not a tireless creative genius. <br /> <br /> You can let a player at your table say &quot;I'm chosen of Ahlat, here is the charmset I devised based on solar level charms... Uh I don't know why he gave me this power... Now lets get going on that diplomatic peacemaking mission to Coral.&quot; You can even wing it and make a fun story out of that. Maybe peacemaking in the West weakens Siakal giving Ahlat some leverage on a problem he needs desperately to solve. I'm not saying it can't happen. I'm just trying to lend arguments to those trying to figure out a way to reign it in a bit in case they fell the need to.<br /> <br /> Maybe I've expressed myself poorly, so I'll clarify. <br /> <br /> I'm unconcerned with crunch, as there is absolutely none to discuss nor read into anything. All I'm discussing is setting fluff.<br /> <br /> People were expressing concern over Exigents being the go to splat and overriding setting precepts. I'm exposing my point of view of why that won't happen in setting. PCs are a different ballpark, people should play however they want, I'm not here to discuss this.<br /> <br /> We have these points (that the devs may change anytime anyways), that I know of, feel free to add new ones or challenge any of them:<br /> <br /> A. The first Exaltations were subject to the Law of Diminishments.<br /> <br /> B. Exigency is a way for gods unable (or unwilling, etc) to Exalt someone on their own to petition The UCS for a champion.<br /> <br /> C. There is a way to get around from The UCS' petition process.<br /> <br /> D. The only example of Exaltation through Exigency that we have shows a god being diminished to the point of ceasing to be.<br /> <br /> Now, you (Zelbinnean) can point out how my extrapolations are illogical, thats what I'm here for. But simply saying they are not based in fact is pretty poor conversation, what facts are these you are working with or that I fail to see? Seems like you think Exigency is a free miracle, care to indicate what tidbit you are extrapolating from to get to this? Or are your assumptions not based in facts?<br /> <br /> Again, no crunch, only setting fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T14:32:16-07:00","id":698977,"title":"","content":"Various probably tl:dr-ish and tangential thoughts:<br /> <br /> With tiers, yes, Isator describes it well. Even when we talked about tiers it was often prefaced with &quot;Assuming two Exalted of exactly the same focus, trying to go about things exactly the same way, opposing one...&quot;. Which there is an element of &quot;How often does that really happen?&quot;.<br /> <br /> I have to admit I found some of the anti-tier thinking a little annoying back in the day, when there was the whole &quot;But... ah, what if you burned down the building he was in rather than let him fight you? Where are the tiers now?! Huh.&quot; stuff.<br /> <br /> Basically because that extreme fundamentally dodged out of the idea that maybe you wanted to have a kung fu duel with the guy, if you're playing a martial artist in a kung fu game. But definitely the idea that conflicts are really not constrained in their approach to really simple scenarios, has a lot of relevance.<br /> <br /> With Exigents and tiers, specifically, especially the idea of tiers is kind of wonkier than normal, because Exigents are the place where people will explore weird mechanics which are of course sometimes much better and much worse than they expect, in different situations, which you'll inevitably have to wing and adjust as you go along. (For the inescapable fighting game analogy, there are some always characters who are sort of generally bad against most, but then have amazing matchups against characters who are formally considered &quot;strong&quot;.)<br /> <br /> And there's the human element - if the Exigent player shoots for a Celestial level of characters (as much as tiers are reductive) and then just is more creative in coming up with useful Charms and then using them than a bunch of Solars he's playing with then, that's another thing where you just have to deal. It's like we're going to tell them to stop making their character so cool or anything. <br /> <br /> (Thinking about this thread a little at work today, I was musing about an Exigent of a god of nets and waves, with a powerful fisherman god mythos to draw on like you might expect in fantasy with a seafaring focus. Now what if I was shooting for Celestial level with that character, but the Charm ideas came thick and fast and really did just happen to end up being a bit more effective than that, and through luck and feeling really inspired by the character, even more effective in my hands? I've no clue how that would hash out other than to accept that the character is just like that).<br /> <br /> Re: the ongoing discussion with TGUEIROS, it's not that I think you're wrong TGUEIROS, just it is a maybe some bits of an extreme interpretation to go towards, even if it's not illogical at all. Of course we are all doing Kremlinology a little here. Compared to what you think, it is more that there could well be quite a bit more latitude for individual miraculous results that aren't expected by a given god or UCS, as the fusion of essence of the hero, god and sun becomes more than expected. Or for the UCS to be overwhelmed by his own passion in granting power. Or for the UCS to be very clever and calculating (and you know he also happens to be the deeply respected primus inter pares and commander of these five sort of awesome ladies with peerlessly vast insight into the future, and this other lady who's about the slyest and tricksiest thing there ever was) that you don't know why he's devoted so much power to a particular chosen (in practice, until the player pulls something out, eventually). It has to suit the game though, of course, so of course you'll roll with what suits you.<br /> <br /> One thing I found interesting and sort of on this note, on the What We Know page, was that John Morke noted that the list of reasons Tiresias gave for Siakal seeking an Exaltation were awesome... for a Black Market Exaltation, but illegal as shit for the official Exigency. And at the same time when Tiresias asked further about this, part of the comment was &quot;It has more to do with virtuosity than pragmatism.&quot;.<br /> <br /> So the idea that Exaltations of Exigency are necessarily because the god has this exactly calculating scheme to benefit themselves and where the Exigent has this exact role in that... Maybe not that much.<br /> <br /> The gods of Heaven are the divine and numinous, beyond human, breathtaking and baffling and noble, yet incessantly brawling, competitive and greedy gods of pagan myth (or at least as evoked by sword and sorcery). For all that, there is a divine plan and order to Heaven and a dignity to the offices of state. Yes, the gods are calculating, and the Sidereals are cunning, and even the Unconquered Sun is canny to realpolitik, but Heaven ostensibly has a duty to this mortal world, and the Exigency is a gift from the sun to the gods to make a better world (I suspect). It is not the equivalent of guns and money on the public purse to put in the hands of any mercenary to further the goals and schemes of a petty god. Heaven is public spirited, even through it's corruption, even if it's spirits are not public spirited. There is still some belief for the gods, or I'd like to think there is in 3e, in the dignity of a Celestial Order that stands for something.<br /> <br /> Old Ahlat is cunning, but not depthlessly so, and when he moves to seek the Exigence, the Sun can know if it is because he looks on his lands, and wider than that to the world and sees they cry out for a hero, or if he is merely looking for a mighty thug to prop up his power.<br /> <br /> (Not that I know any more about it than you guys, just kind of going off on one here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T15:54:20-07:00","id":699050,"title":"","content":"It is the Divine Flame of <i><b>Exigency</b></i>. It is not &quot;just&quot; a divine miracle, its very nature may be to answer the most desperate of needs and noblest of causes, as filtered through the Essence of the Sun and his Virtues and view of what is a noble cause and what is not.<br /> <br /> So perhaps there is no equation of energy or motes you can sum up to predict the power tier of the Exigent. Perhaps the Exigence responds to the need and nobility of the cause with commensurate power, or with just what is needed and no more or less than that. And perhaps how a non-living miraculous nebula of divine Essence &quot;judges&quot; this is even more mysterious than how Sol decides who to exalt with his own gift of Essence, which is already mysterious and will be more mysterious in 3E.<br /> <br /> This is, honestly, about how I expect it to go in the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T22:37:04-07:00","id":699505,"title":"","content":"You see Ghost, I basically agree with everything on your post. The tier thing is basically a easy way to talk about power potential. Some are concerned that by Exigents being mentioned to be able to reach the height of power in the setting under specific situations is going to distort their games. Maybe they have pushy players that are all gonna make a chosen of something that is very powerful and supposedly unhindered by the Great Curse and social consequences of being Anathema. I'm just trying to have a conversation on why this isn't the case and why the setting isn't itself overrun with Exigents.<br /> <br /> The whole bit about calculated move vs virtuous need I understand and agree with. I even gave an example of it in a previous post, ie the desperate gambler betting his rent money to get his daughter her meds. The money thing is just figure of speech, I understand all the mystical and mysterious wrappings that Exigency is enclosed by.<br /> <br /> The Exigency is a Miracle, capital M and all. All I'm saying is that it isn't a free one. A sacrifice must be made, the price must be paid. What that price this is, while we can muse about it (which is what I was doing) we don't exactly know, and maybe never will, even when the book is out (another thing I mentioned on a previous post). And that is a good enough reason for the setting not to be overrun by these guys and a good enough reason to handle disruptive character concepts that don't give anything to the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T22:49:00-07:00","id":699509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=699050#post699050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is the Divine Flame of <i><b>Exigency</b></i>. It is not &quot;just&quot; a divine miracle, its very nature may be to answer the most desperate of needs and noblest of causes, as filtered through the Essence of the Sun and his Virtues and view of what is a noble cause and what is not.<br /> <br /> So perhaps there is no equation of energy or motes you can sum up to predict the power tier of the Exigent. Perhaps the Exigence responds to the need and nobility of the cause with commensurate power, or with just what is needed and no more or less than that. And perhaps how a non-living miraculous nebula of divine Essence &quot;judges&quot; this is even more mysterious than how Sol decides who to exalt with his own gift of Essence, which is already mysterious and will be more mysterious in 3E.<br /> <br /> This is, honestly, about how I expect it to go in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>All is colored by individual perceptions. It may be that because of my job the cost component part stood out as essential to me, it makes sense and resonates with that part of me. It may be that for you it is not essential and it was part only of the stories we know about, and other stories may be told without this part.<br /> <br /> We have very little to go on here, so any discussion on it is just thought exercise for the people involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T09:27:59-07:00","id":699886,"title":"","content":"I didn't mean that there isn't a cost. There's always a cost to the god.<br /> <br /> I said that I don't think you can <i><b>mathematically calculate</b></i> the power or mote pool of the Exigent based on the number of dots of Essence the god sacrificed to empower them or the number of successes on their prayer roll to beseech Sol Invictus. I don't believe there will be an official equation or even an implication that there's any predictable, linear correlation between what the god loses and what their champion gains. I think the source and nature of the Flame of Exigency will completely overwhelm any such correspondence that might theoretically exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-13-2015, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T15:16:43-07:00","id":700174,"title":"","content":"I would expect a degree of correlation, but I agree not to a degree that it can be exactly calculated predictably at all. I just expect a god who dies exalting an exigent is more likely to turn out a more powerful being than a god of the same rough rank and essence who does not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T03:44:34-07:00","id":700629,"title":"","content":"Speaking of elementals, something that always piqued my interest though spread as loose tidbits across Roll of Glorious Divinity is the idea that certain qualities of spirits and elementals as a whole can and do change through times like most, if not all Masks, were destroyed in some time in the ancient past and due to association/correlation with the element of water a number of them never came back, actually mixing into parts of what would be Water Children instead, how the Amabossar are elementals of a fire like the element never was supposed to be, in a time when its associations and those of another element (earth, i think) temporarily changed places due to the spiritual fallout/upheaval of the Contagion &amp; Balorian Crusade, Serpent-&amp;-Eggs changing masters (and general temperament) in some time in the past, the fact that a number of elemental races seem to have no connection with regeneration of Creation's essence patterns but the personal fancies of individual lesser elemental dragons and so on.<br /> <br /> I would like to know if anyone has noticed and tinkered somewhat with that kind of stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T04:54:49-07:00","id":700702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=699505#post699505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole bit about calculated move vs virtuous need I understand and agree with. I even gave an example of it in a previous post, ie the desperate gambler betting his rent money to get his daughter her meds. The money thing is just figure of speech, I understand all the mystical and mysterious wrappings that Exigency is enclosed by.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the issues I see with &quot;need&quot; and &quot;virtue of need&quot; is how the Exigence can be tricked, or divine fire be stolen and sold on the black marketed those whose requests for it wouldn't be granted, or perverted as a &quot;dirty bomb.&quot; How exactly those things can happen when the root word refers to great need (presumably great need sympathized with by UCS) has yet to be seen, and to me reflects on the fact that UCS is neither omniscient nor omnipotent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T04:58:17-07:00","id":700705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=700702#post700702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the issues I see with &quot;need&quot; and &quot;virtue of need&quot; is how the Exigence can be tricked, or divine fire be stolen and sold on the black marketed those whose requests for it wouldn't be granted, or perverted as a &quot;dirty bomb.&quot; How exactly those things can happen when the root word refers to great need (presumably great need sympathized with by UCS) has yet to be seen, and to me reflects on the fact that UCS is neither omniscient nor omnipotent.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All of a sudden, I'm thinking it can often play out a lot like the beginning of Kill Six Billion Demons...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T05:32:54-07:00","id":700716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=700702#post700702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the issues I see with &quot;need&quot; and &quot;virtue of need&quot; is how the Exigence can be tricked, or divine fire be stolen and sold on the black marketed those whose requests for it wouldn't be granted, or perverted as a &quot;dirty bomb.&quot; How exactly those things can happen when the root word refers to great need (presumably great need sympathized with by UCS) has yet to be seen, and to me reflects on the fact that UCS is neither omniscient nor omnipotent.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Need&quot; can confound itself quite easily with &quot;want&quot; depending on individual, not to mention not every need has to be particularly just or positive. On itself speaks far more of &quot;why would you sacrifice part (or the whole) of yourself to bring a demigod-weapon to act into your place and name and how far would one go to make it so?&quot; than anything i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T09:27:49-07:00","id":706996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=697919#post697919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to play a Chosen of Death but can't come up with why Thanatos, Supreme God of Death, cut a out a hefty chunk of his soul to empower you then you are going to be the Chosen of Mr Gravedirt, God of Those Who Died When They Were Burying Another Person. And your power level is Terrestrial, at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really dislike this.<br /> The kind of person who needs their custom Exalts to be Solar level would not be stopped by this, all this will do is put people off using Mr Gravedirt as their patron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T10:03:21-07:00","id":707042,"title":"","content":"I sincerely hope the power gap between Solar and Terrestrial level will be narrow enough that these worries over relative balance of Exigents will not be relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T13:24:13-07:00","id":707355,"title":"","content":"My experience is that the fluff and the white room mentality played a greater role in things.<br /> If a Celestial Exalt was defeated by a Dragon-Blooded (or a group of mortals) using good tactics and playing to their strengths then they were invariably branded an idiot for not having the charms and combos they needed to negate their opponent's tactics.<br /> <br /> Too much of the discourse appeared to be controlled by people for whom the game was a purely theoretical exercise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T19:35:01-07:00","id":740619,"title":"","content":"So now that we've got the core book to provide both a sample Exigent and a Field Guardian, what do you think Strawmaiden Janest can do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T20:42:55-07:00","id":740755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695164#post695164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the issues with elementals being able to create Exigents is that everyone would make the Chosen of a lesser elemental dragon who is just a DB but with Solar-tier power. Gods tend to create more original and interesting Exigents.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do that anyway: Gods of trees, or of forests, or of X plant, or a combination there of, for wood aspect, gods of lakes or of rivers or of storms for water aspects, gods of the wind, or of deserts, or of storms for the wind aspect, gods of mountains or of deserts or of mudslides or of mines for earth aspects, or gods of volcnoes or ash clouds, or of a forest that brurned down for fire aspect... Okay, completly honest I'm having trouble coming up with deities that could create and exigent that could pass for strait up fire.<br /> <br /> Or all of the Above for some kind of super omni-elemntal psudo-dragonblooded Dirty bomb exigent.<br /> <br /> The hard part is coming up with a god or gods who's specific power set over their domain is close enough to a dragonbloodeds elemental powers for the Exigenrt to pass for a Dragonblood","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T21:36:51-07:00","id":740869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=706996#post706996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really dislike this.<br /> The kind of person who needs their custom Exalts to be Solar level would not be stopped by this, all this will do is put people off using Mr Gravedirt as their patron.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't there a thread a while back about &quot;Joke Exigents&quot; like the chosen of the god of Buffulo Dung, and one of the Devs(I forgot which) commented that such an Exigent would actually be incredibly powerful and versatile?<br /> <br /> I honestly think that &quot;how powerful an exigent&quot; is will depend more on what the god is and how much of themselves that they give up than what the God's power level is, even if that might be a factor.<br /> <br /> I mean, if the Exigents are the Chosen of the Lesser gods and most are unique-or at least only one of them at a time, <i>and </i>these lesser gods can potentially make something solar powered, than logically you wouldn't need a High Ranking Celestial Deity to make something stronger than a Terrestrial. I mean, if they're only making the one, it won't take nearly as much energy as making hundreds.<br /> <br /> So I could totally see Mr. Gravedirt making a celestial or solar leveled champion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T22:52:26-07:00","id":740959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=740869#post740869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there a thread a while back about &quot;Joke Exigents&quot; like the chosen of the god of Buffulo Dung, and one of the Devs(I forgot which) commented that such an Exigent would actually be incredibly powerful and versatile?<br /> <br /> I honestly think that &quot;how powerful an exigent&quot; is will depend more on what the god is and how much of themselves that they give up than what the God's power level is, even if that might be a factor.<br /> <br /> I mean, if the Exigents are the Chosen of the Lesser gods and most are unique-or at least only one of them at a time, <i>and </i>these lesser gods can potentially make something solar powered, than logically you wouldn't need a High Ranking Celestial Deity to make something stronger than a Terrestrial. I mean, if they're only making the one, it won't take nearly as much energy as making hundreds.<br /> <br /> So I could totally see Mr. Gravedirt making a celestial or solar leveled champion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understood that.<br /> My point was that the suggestion by TGUEIROS would do nothing to stop people from making arbitrarily powerful Exigents and particularly if it was framed like that it would probably only deter people from making the Exalts of weaker gods.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T23:01:32-07:00","id":740975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695105#post695105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said I bet if you want elementals or demons to have some weird way to Exalt people, the Exigents book will provide you with a good way to mechanically implement that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is precisely what I was thinking. I reckon the book will pass the fire so that I have the guidelines to create whatever the hell Exalted level blokes to tag along with my circles be they Curse Marked Struggler Berserkers like Guts, to Keybladers, to Mummies!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T23:05:21-07:00","id":740977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=695187#post695187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There was. One was an Elemental that ascended to greater poeer. The other, from DotFA (something else that book screwed up) was some sort of ctjonic god that was accidently released.<br /> <br /> Seems the writers of previous editions didnt talk to each other much when worldbuilding. I hope the current dev team is more careful</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually its just they forgot that Elementals were relatively knew to Creation, a common mistake as it was even reflected in the Dragon Kings' Paths where they knew how to summon Elementals before they were a Thing and Autochthon had Lesser Elemental Dragons before the Primordial War... I'm glad they adjusted it to have Elementals be Ancient spirits and not new Digi/Pokemons popping up in the First Age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T08:38:28-07:00","id":741927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/695059-can-elementals-create-exigents?p=740959#post740959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understood that.<br /> My point was that the suggestion by TGUEIROS would do nothing to stop people from making arbitrarily powerful Exigents and particularly if it was framed like that it would probably only deter people from making the Exalts of weaker gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going off of what you said to make a point.<br /> <br /> TGUEIROS says that you need an Incarnae level deity to make an exigent over Terrestrial Level.<br /> You say no you don't, and even if you did it'd just mean people wouldn't choose lesser deities as patrons<br /> I follow up your point by saying that it's been confirmed that a minor deity can produce an incredibly powerful exigent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}